# Copy to .env and adjust if needed, then: uvicorn main:app --env-file .env

# --- Bind address. Keep 127.0.0.1: a dashboard that can place no orders is
# --- still a dashboard that shows your account and position size.
CHARON_HOST=127.0.0.1
CHARON_PORT=8787

# --- Optional shared secret. When set, every /api/* call except /api/health
# --- and /api/logs must send X-Charon-Token with this value.
# --- Leave unset for a single-user desktop bound to loopback.
# CHARON_TOKEN=change-me

# --- Cross-origin access. Leave unset for the normal install, where the
# --- dashboard is served by this same process at http://127.0.0.1:8787/ and
# --- needs no CORS header at all.
# ---
# --- Set it ONLY when the UI is served from somewhere else -- a Vercel
# --- deployment, a second machine -- and list the exact origins, comma
# --- separated, scheme and port included. Origins match literally; there are
# --- no wildcards.
# ---
# --- Two warnings that matter more than the syntax:
# ---
# --- 1. A page on the public internet cannot call 127.0.0.1: that is the
# ---    BROWSER's loopback, not your PC's. To expose this bridge to a remote
# ---    UI you also need a tunnel (Cloudflare Tunnel, Tailscale, ngrok) and
# ---    CHARON_HOST set to the interface the tunnel reaches.
# --- 2. The moment you do, set CHARON_TOKEN as well. This console shows your
# ---    account balance, your position sizes and can queue orders. An origin
# ---    allowlist stops OTHER pages from reading it; it does not
# ---    authenticate the person using yours.
# CHARON_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://charon.example.vercel.app

# --- Override the MT5 Common\Files location. Only needed when the terminal
# --- lives somewhere unusual (portable install, Wine, second user account).
# CHARON_COMMON_DIR=C:\Users\you\AppData\Roaming\MetaQuotes\Terminal\Common\Files

# --- Broker symbol affixes. Many brokers name EURUSD "EURUSD.a", "EURUSDm"
# --- or "mEURUSD"; these tell the symbol picker which part is decoration.
# --- Set them to whatever your terminal actually lists -- see the Market
# --- Watch window -- or leave both unset if it uses the plain name.
# ---
# --- These affect DISPLAY ONLY. A command always carries the exact broker
# --- name, so a wrong value here can never send an order to a symbol the
# --- terminal does not have; it only makes the picker's labels noisy.
# ---
# --- They do NOT need to be set for /api/order to find the right chart: a
# --- ticket naming "EURUSD" resolves to the live "EURUSD.a" on its own, by
# --- recognising the trailing tag on the name the EA publishes. Set these
# --- when a prefix/suffix should also be hidden from the displayed label.
# CHARON_SYMBOL_PREFIX=m
# CHARON_SYMBOL_SUFFIX=.a
